# The same eight solids as 'AeroAssembly.assy', placed where they can actually
# be put together. 'AeroAssembly.assy' is the unedited record of what
# 'pc import assembly' read out of 'AeroAssembly.step'; this file is that record
# with its three interferences resolved, and every difference between the two is
# a placement, commented below. Not one part file differs.
#
# See 'docs.intro' in ../partcad.yaml for what each of the three overlaps turned
# out to be and why these are the corrections.
name: AeroAssembly_buildable
description: >-
  The imported AeroAssembly with its three interferences resolved: the mirrored
  frame half moved onto the bolt pattern it is meant to bolt to, the cap lifted
  clear of the plate by the 0.751923 mm its front feet overhang, and every
  placement written at the precision the STEP file actually holds instead of the
  five decimals the importer rounds to.
links:
  # Unchanged from the import except for the extra digits: this half already
  # bolted up flush. Its four 3 mm holes are coaxial with the plate's front
  # flange (x = -102.040610, y = -45.2/-42.2/-30.2/-27.2) and its bolt face is
  # flat against the flange's underside at z = 69.691086.
  - type: assembly
    name: AeroFrameAssembly
    links:
      - type: part
        name: AeroFrameAssembly_solid1
        part: AeroAssembly_assy_example/AeroFrameAssembly_solid1
        location: [[-69.134226869844, -87.080855661874, 82.881290119571], [1.0, 0.0,
            0.0], 0.0]
      - type: part
        name: AeroFrameAssembly_solid2
        part: AeroAssembly_assy_example/AeroFrameAssembly_solid2
        location: [[-69.134226869844, -87.080855661874, 82.881290119571], [1.0, 0.0,
            0.0], 0.0]
      - type: part
        name: AeroFrameAssembly_solid3
        part: AeroAssembly_assy_example/AeroFrameAssembly_solid3
        location: [[-128.617172447944, 53.052923677092, 75.225092331764], [0.129428307996,
            -0.129428307996, -0.98310560276], 90.976200401604]
  - type: part
    name: AeroFrame_Plate
    part: AeroAssembly_assy_example/AeroFrame_Plate
    location: [[-76.86294015592, -86.19998835248, 80.297688179203], [1.0, 0.0, 0.0],
      0.0]
  # Raised by 0.751923190 mm in z (80.297688179203 -> 81.049611369203).
  #
  # The cap stands on the plate on four feet. The two rear ones (8 x 10 mm)
  # land exactly on the plate's rear flange at z = 131.885499. The two front
  # ones (6 x 10 mm) reach down to z = 75.939163 while the front flange's top
  # face is at z = 76.691086, so each of them was 0.751923 mm inside the plate:
  # 6 x 10 x 0.751923 = 45.115 mm^3 twice, the 90.231 mm^3 the check reported.
  #
  # That is a defect in the cap part, not in its placement - the feet are
  # modelled 5.000 mm and 6.000 mm tall against faces 0.751923 mm apart, and no
  # rigid motion of one part seats all four. Trimming the front feet would mean
  # editing the imported STEP, which would stop it being the imported STEP, so
  # what this file does instead is the least motion that takes metal out of
  # metal: the cap seats on its front feet and stands 0.751923 mm clear on the
  # rear ones, where nothing fastens through and a shim takes it up.
  - type: part
    name: AeroFrame_Cap
    part: AeroAssembly_assy_example/AeroFrame_Cap
    location: [[-76.86294015592, -86.19998835248, 81.049611369203], [1.0, 0.0, 0.0],
      0.0]
  # Moved by (+7.728713286, -3.380867309, +2.583601940) mm, as one rigid body.
  #
  # The plate's front flange carries eight 3 mm holes in two mirrored groups of
  # four, one group per frame half. The half above is bolted through its group;
  # this one missed the other group by exactly that vector, which left it
  # 2.583602 mm clear of the flange at solid2 and 12.998 mm^3 inside the plate
  # at solid1 - a half that is simultaneously floating and buried, which is how
  # a misplaced instance reads rather than a design.
  #
  # The vector is not fitted: it is what puts the four holes on the plate's
  # four. It equals the plate's own origin offset from the frame's,
  # (-7.728713286, +0.880867309, -2.583601940), negated, plus 2.5 mm along -y -
  # the exporter had folded the plate's offset into the mirrored branch. After
  # it, every clearance this half has matches its twin's to the ninth decimal:
  # 0.000000000 mm to the plate at both feet, 7.751923190 and 6.486821381 mm to
  # the cap.
  - type: assembly
    name: MirrorAeroFrameAssembly
    links:
      - type: part
        name: MirrorAeroFrameAssembly_solid1
        part: AeroAssembly_assy_example/MirrorAeroFrameAssembly_solid1
        location: [[-76.862940156, -88.699988352, -75.130484299], [1.0, 0.0, 0.0],
          0.0]
      - type: part
        name: MirrorAeroFrameAssembly_solid2
        part: AeroAssembly_assy_example/MirrorAeroFrameAssembly_solid2
        location: [[-76.862940156, -88.699988352, -75.130484299], [1.0, 0.0, 0.0],
          0.0]
      - type: part
        name: MirrorAeroFrameAssembly_solid3
        part: AeroAssembly_assy_example/MirrorAeroFrameAssembly_solid3
        location: [[-136.345885734, 51.433790987, -67.474286511], [-0.129428307996,
            0.129428307996, -0.98310560276], 90.976200401604]
